Stan's Robot Shop
  https://github.com/instana/robot-shop
  Copyright the Stan's Robot Shop authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  The application source in this repository -- the twelve service
  directories, their Dockerfiles, and the upstream docker-compose files --
  originates here. The microservices, their ports, and the three-tier
  arrangement (web frontend, business services, data stores) are its
  design.

  Modified from upstream in this repository. See the history of any
  service directory for specifics; the substantive changes are:

    dispatch/Dockerfile
      - exec-form CMD replacing shell form, which had caused the container
        to exit immediately with "/bin/sh: 1: [dispatch]: not found"
      - go.mod and go.sum committed, replacing dependency resolution at
        image build time
      - runs as an unprivileged user

    shipping/Dockerfile
      - build stage based on maven:3.8.8-eclipse-temurin-8
      - JVM heap reduced to match the chart's memory limit

    web/default.conf.template
      - upstream hostnames resolved at request time via a resolver
        directive rather than at configuration load

    mysql/Dockerfile
      - MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD set, replacing MYSQL_ALLOW_EMPTY_PASSWORD
      - entrypoint ordering left intact; no functional change

    All services
      - .dockerignore added per build context


iam-veeramalla/three-tier-architecture-demo
  https://github.com/iam-veeramalla/three-tier-architecture-demo
  Copyright the three-tier-architecture-demo authors
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  A fork of instana/robot-shop adding AWS EKS deployment material. The
  EKS/ directory structure and the general shape of the setup steps come
  from here. The documents under EKS/ in this repository were rewritten
  to describe what was actually done, and the chart under EKS/helm/ was
  modified substantially -- see the chart's own README and git history.

  Modified from upstream in this repository:

    EKS/helm/templates/web-service.yaml
      Service type is ClusterIP, configurable via web.serviceType, rather
      than LoadBalancer. Renders the same by default.

    EKS/helm/templates/podsecuritypolicy.yaml
    EKS/helm/templates/clusterrole.yaml
    EKS/helm/templates/clusterrolebinding.yaml
    EKS/helm/templates/serviceaccount.yaml
      Deleted. PodSecurityPolicy was removed in Kubernetes 1.25.

    EKS/helm/templates/{mysql,shipping}-deployment.yaml
      Resource requests are values-driven rather than hardcoded.

    EKS/helm/values.yaml
      mysql and shipping resources; probes; topologySpreadConstraints;
      antiAffinity; podDisruptionBudgets; imagePullSecrets; commonLabels;
      commonAnnotations; dataTier images; web.serviceType

    EKS/helm/values.schema.json
      Added.

    EKS/helm/templates/poddisruptionbudgets.yaml
      Added.

    EKS/01-prerequisites.md through EKS/05-ebs-csi-driver.md
      Rewritten to match the steps actually performed.

    dispatch/docker-compose.yaml
      Removed. Superseded by the root docker-compose.yaml and referring to
      a third party's published images.

    docker-compose-load.yaml
      Removed. Requires a load-gen/ directory that is not part of this
      repository.


